(A width pads a float, a text and a buffer out to that many characters,
 exactly as it pads a number, in every place a format string renders.)

To 'announce the line' with a text called line.
  Print line.

a number called count is 42.
a number called debt is -42.
a float called price is 3.5.
a float called loss is -3.5.
a text called name is "Vox".
a buffer called word is "hi".

(Print position.)
Print "[{count:8}] [{price:8}] [{name:8}] [{word:8}]".
Print "[{debt:08}] [{loss:08}] [{price:08}] [{name:08}]".
Print "[{count:8.2}] [{price:8.2}] [{loss:08.2}]".

(A value as wide as the width, or wider, is printed as it is.)
Print "[{price:3}] [{price:2}] [{name:3}] [{name:1}] [{price:0}] [{name:0}]".

(A text, a buffer, a file and a call argument render the same characters.)
a text called line is "[{count:8}] [{price:8}] [{name:8}] [{word:8}]".
Print line.
a text called signed is "[{loss:08}] [{price:08}] [{name:08}] [{loss:08.2}]".
Print signed.
a buffer called report is 64 bytes in size.
copy "[{price:6}]" to report.
append "[{name:6}]" to report.
Print report.
'announce the line' of "[{price:7.1}] [{name:7}]".
open a file for writing called record at "./a_width_pads_a_float.txt".
Write "[{price:6}] [{name:6}]\n" to record.
Close record.
open a file for reading called stored at "./a_width_pads_a_float.txt".
a buffer called 'stored line' is 64 bytes in size.
Read line from stored into 'stored line'.
Print 'stored line' without newline.
Close stored.
Delete the file "./a_width_pads_a_float.txt".

(A list element whose type is known only when the program runs.)
a list called mixed is [1, "two", 3.5].
Print "[{element 2 of mixed:5}] [{element 3 of mixed:5}]".
a text called tagged is "[{element 2 of mixed:5}] [{element 3 of mixed:5}]".
Print tagged.

(The same hole, every time round a loop.)
For each number from 1 to 3,
  Print "[{price:5}{name:5}]".

(A padded value that does not fit a fixed buffer keeps what fits.)
a buffer called small is 6 bytes in size.
copy "[{name:9}]" to small.
On error Print "the padded name does not fit in six bytes".
Print small.

(A float longer than a page is padded too: 4200 characters, ten of them fill.)
a buffer called long is 8192 bytes in size.
copy "{price:4200.4188}" to long.
Print long's length.
Print "{price:4200.4188}".
